/* Central style rules for MatchaEditor widgets.
 *
 * Colors here should stay in step with the dark QPalette applied in Theme.cpp - this file is
 * only for the handful of things a QPalette can't express (per-instance axis colors, bold
 * section labels, a widget-specific text alignment). Anything a QPalette already covers (window/
 * base/button/text/highlight colors) belongs there, not duplicated here.
 *
 * Widgets opt into a rule by object name or a dynamic property, not by literal color/font values
 * baked into their own C++ - see FieldLabel.h's ApplySquishPolicy neighbors, ComponentBoxWidget,
 * Vec3ControlWidget/Vec4ControlWidget, and InspectorPanel's CreateSectionLabel for the setObjectName/
 * setProperty calls this file's selectors match against.
 */

QToolTip {
    color: #e0e0e0;
    background-color: #3c3c3c;
    border: 1px solid #545454;
}

/* ComponentBoxWidget's collapsible header button - left-aligned title instead of Fusion's
 * default centered QPushButton text. */
QPushButton#ComponentHeaderButton {
    text-align: left;
}

/* InspectorPanel::CreateSectionLabel - names a group of fields (e.g. "Perspective" above
 * CameraComponent's FOV/Near/Far) with the same size as a normal label, just bolded. */
QLabel#SectionLabel {
    font-weight: bold;
}

/* Read-only info rows (mesh handle, script count) in InspectorPanel. */
QLabel#ReadOnlyInfoLabel {
    padding: 2px;
}

/* Vec3ControlWidget/Vec4ControlWidget axis labels - Unity-accurate axis colors (Red/Green/Blue/
 * White for X/Y/Z/W). Centralized here via the "axis" property instead of a hex string passed
 * into each widget, so both control widgets (and any future one) share a single source of truth. */
QLabel[axis="x"] {
    color: #ff5555;
    font-weight: bold;
}

QLabel[axis="y"] {
    color: #55ff55;
    font-weight: bold;
}

QLabel[axis="z"] {
    color: #5555ff;
    font-weight: bold;
}

QLabel[axis="w"] {
    color: #cccccc;
    font-weight: bold;
}
